      "updated": 1792422479646,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The kerne's attributes say what's allowed. The\nhost's LaunchConfig2D says what actually happens this run.\n\ndomain = 2: a 2D launch, where the grid has x and y.\n\nblock = (16, 16, 1): 16 threads across (x = col), 16 down (y = row), 1 deep (z).\nThat's 256 per block.\n\nHost config: grid(80, 37) blocks, worked out from this picture's\nsize, which only the host knows. Block (16, 16) must match the\ncontract, and z is automatically 1. The 0 is bytes of\nshared memory, which we don't use.\n\nThe contract checks the shape of the launch, not whether it fits the data.\nCovering the picture is on us (div_ceil and the kernel's bounds checks).\n\nlaunch_bounds isn't a launch check. It lets the compiler\nplan resources. ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The kerne's attributes say what's allowed. The\nhost's LaunchConfig2D says what actually happens this run.\n\ndomain = 2: a 2D launch, where the grid has x and y.\n\nblock = (16, 16, 1): 16 threads across (x = col), 16 down (y = row), 1 deep (z).\nThat's 256 per block.\n\nHost config: grid(80, 37) blocks, worked out from this picture's\nsize, which only the host knows. Block (16, 16) must match the\ncontract, and z is automatically 1. The 0 is bytes of\nshared memory, which we don't use.\n\nThe contract checks the shape of the launch, not whether it fits the data.\nCovering the picture is on us (div_ceil and the kernel's bounds checks).\n\nlaunch_bounds isn't a launch check. It lets the compiler\nplan resources. ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
